---
// Architecture Component for MirDB Homepage
// Displays a visual diagram of the LSM tree data flow and explanation
---

<section id="architecture" class="py-16 px-4 bg-slate-800">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-10 text-center">How MirDB Works</h2>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-start">
      <!-- Architecture Diagram -->
      <div
        data-testid="architecture-diagram"
        role="img"
        aria-label="MirDB LSM tree architecture diagram showing data flow from write requests through WAL, Memtable, and SSTable levels"
        class="bg-slate-900 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-lg"
      >
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
          <!-- Write Request -->
          <div class="diagram-row">
            <div class="bg-blue-900 border-2 border-blue-500 rounded-lg px-6 py-3 text-center min-w-[200px]">
              <span class="block font-semibold text-blue-300">Write Request</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="text-slate-500 text-2xl">&#8595;</div>

          <!-- WAL -->
          <div class="diagram-row">
            <div class="bg-pink-900 border-2 border-pink-500 rounded-lg px-6 py-3 text-center min-w-[200px]">
              <span class="block font-semibold text-pink-300">WAL</span>
              <span class="block text-xs text-pink-400 mt-1">Write-Ahead Log</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="text-slate-500 text-2xl">&#8595;</div>

          <!-- Memtable -->
          <div class="diagram-row flex items-center gap-4">
            <div class="bg-green-900 border-2 border-green-500 rounded-lg px-6 py-3 text-center min-w-[200px]">
              <span class="block font-semibold text-green-300">Memtable</span>
              <span class="block text-xs text-green-400 mt-1">In-memory Skip List</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <div class="text-slate-500 text-2xl">&#8595;</div>
            <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 italic">when full</span>
          </div>

          <!-- Immutable Memtables -->
          <div class="diagram-row">
            <div class="bg-orange-900 border-2 border-orange-500 rounded-lg px-6 py-3 text-center min-w-[200px]">
              <span class="block font-semibold text-orange-300">Immutable Memtables</span>
              <span class="block text-xs text-orange-400 mt-1">Queue awaiting flush</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <div class="text-slate-500 text-2xl">&#8595;</div>
            <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 italic">minor compaction</span>
          </div>

          <!-- Level 0 SSTables -->
          <div class="diagram-row">
            <div class="bg-purple-900 border-2 border-purple-400 rounded-lg px-6 py-3 text-center min-w-[200px]">
              <span class="block font-semibold text-purple-300">Level 0 SSTables</span>
              <span class="block text-xs text-purple-400 mt-1">Recently flushed, may overlap</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <div class="text-slate-500 text-2xl">&#8595;</div>
            <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 italic">major compaction</span>
          </div>

          <!-- Level 1+ SSTables -->
          <div class="diagram-row">
            <div class="bg-purple-800 border-2 border-purple-300 rounded-lg px-6 py-3 text-center min-w-[200px]">
              <span class="block font-semibold text-purple-200">Level 1+ SSTables</span>
              <span class="block text-xs text-purple-300 mt-1">Sorted, non-overlapping</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- LSM Explanation -->
      <div data-testid="lsm-explanation" class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-orange-500">Log-Structured Merge Tree</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          MirDB uses an <strong class="text-white">LSM (Log-Structured Merge)</strong> tree architecture,
          which is optimized for write-heavy workloads. All writes first go to the
          <strong class="text-white">Write-Ahead Log (WAL)</strong> for durability, then to an
          in-memory <strong class="text-white">Memtable</strong> for fast access.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          When the Memtable fills up, it becomes immutable and is flushed to disk as an
          <strong class="text-white">SSTable (Sorted String Table)</strong>. Background compaction
          processes merge and sort these SSTables across levels, maintaining read performance
          while optimizing storage efficiency.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          This design provides excellent write performance, crash recovery through WAL, and
          efficient reads through bloom filters and block indexes in each SSTable.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-6 p-4 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg border border-slate-700">
          <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Key Benefits</h4>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-300 text-sm">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-green-400">&#10003;</span>
              <span>High write throughput through sequential I/O</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-green-400">&#10003;</span>
              <span>Crash recovery via Write-Ahead Logging</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-green-400">&#10003;</span>
              <span>Efficient space utilization through compaction</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-green-400">&#10003;</span>
              <span>Optimized reads with bloom filters</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
